<title>USA: USDA 7-State and U.S. Cattle on Feed.</title>
<headline>USDA 7-State and U.S. Cattle on Feed.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA cattle on feed,</p>
<p>1,000-plus head feedlots (data in 1,000 head):</p>
<p>    7 MAJOR STATES --  Pct----1997-----1996     1995</p>
<p> On Feed April 1	 107   8,904    8,286    8,328</p>
<p>During March:</p>
<p> -Placed on Feed	 102   1,694    1,666    1,681</p>
<p> -Marketed		 101   1,497    1,476    1,513</p>
<p> -Other Disappearance  111	62	 56	 67</p>
<p> On Feed March 1	 108   8,769    8,152    8,227</p>
<p>The seven major states are Arizona, California, Colorado, Iowa,</p>
<p>Kansas, Nebraska and Texas.</p>
<p>USDA cattle on feed in the United States (1,000-plus head feedlots, data in 1,000 head):</p>
<p>    U.S. TOTAL --	Pct----1997-----1996</p>
<p> On Feed April 1	 106  10,391    9,812</p>
<p>During March:</p>
<p> -Placed on Feed	 101   1,966    1,948</p>
<p> -Marketed		 100   1,764    1,756</p>
<p> -Other Disappearance  113	86	 76</p>
<p> On Feed March 1	 106  10,275    9,696</p>
<p>Note-On feed data for U.S. and 7 states include cattle placed on feed after quarter's start and marketed before quarter's start.</p>
</text>
